    "Full API spec": "Public API and import rules\n\nPackage: video_player\n- video_player.__init__ re-exports: ValidationError, StateError, NotFoundError; Media; ManualClock; Playlist; Player; PlaybackState.\n- Import graph must be acyclic: errors -> media -> playlist -> player; clock is orthogonal and imported by player only; tests and Main.py import from video_player or submodules without creating cycles.\n\nExceptions (video_player.errors)\n- class ValidationError(Exception): raised for invalid inputs and configuration.\n- class StateError(ValidationError): raised for invalid state transitions (e.g., play with empty playlist).\n- class NotFoundError(ValidationError): raised when addressing non-existent playlist indices/items.\n\nEntity: Media (video_player.media)\n- class Media:\n  - __init__(self, id: str, title: str, duration_seconds: float, metadata: Optional[dict] = None)\n    - id: non-empty str\n    - title: non-empty str\n    - duration_seconds: float > 0\n    - metadata: optional dict; stored as a shallow copy; object is immutable after construction (no setters; attributes may be read-only via properties or by convention).\n  - Attributes (public, read-only): id, title, duration_seconds, metadata (a shallow-copied dict or {})\n  - Errors: ValidationError for invalid field types/values.\n\nClock: ManualClock (video_player.clock)\n- class ManualClock:\n  - now(self) -> float: returns accumulated clock time in seconds.\n  - add_tick_listener(self, fn: Callable[[float], None]) -> None: registers a listener to receive tick deltas; idempotent add2026-09-13 01:48:02.629 | INFO     | metagpt.utils.token_counter:count_input_tokens:396 - Warning: model gpt-5 not found in tiktoken. Using cl100k_base encoding.
