 allowed; listener called synchronously on tick in registration order.\n  - remove_tick_listener(self, fn) -> None: unregisters a previously added listener; no-op if not present.\n  - tick(self, delta_seconds: float) -> None: advances clock by delta_seconds (> 0) and synchronously notifies listeners via fn(delta_seconds). Raises ValidationError if delta_seconds <= 0.\n\nPlaylist (video_player.playlist)\n- class Playlist:\n  - __init__(self, items: list[Media]): stores an immutable snapshot list of Media; initial _current_index is 0 if non-empty else None.\n  - is_empty(self) -> bool: True if no items.\n  - size(self) -> int: number of items.\n  - current(self) -> Media | None: current Media if selected else None.\n  - select(self, index: int) -> Media: selects and returns item at index; raises NotFoundError for out-of-range; sets current index to index.\n  - next(self) -> Media | None: if empty, return None; if at last item, keep last and return None; otherwise advance index by 1 and return the new current item.\n  - previous(self) -> Media | None: if empty, return None; if at first item, keep first and return None; otherwise decrement index by 1 and return the new current item.\n  - Invariants: indices are 0-based; navigation does not wrap; selection maintains bounds.\n\nPlaybackState (video_player.player)\n- enum-like class PlaybackState with three members: STOPPED, PLAYING, PAUSED. Comparable by identity or value; string reprs stable.\n\nPlayer (video_player.player)\n- class Player:\n  - __init__(self, playlist: Playlist, clock: ManualClock): subscribes an internal _on_tick listener to clock; initializes state STOPPED, position 0.0, volume 1.0, muted False. If playlist not empty, current selection is as in Playlist (index 0 by default).\n  - state(self) -> PlaybackState: returns current playback state.\n  - current_media(self) -> Media | None: returns playlist.current().\n  - position_seconds(self) -> float: current position within current media in seconds; 0.0 when no selection.\n  - duration_seconds(self) -> float: duration of current media in seconds; 0.0 when no selection.\n  - play(self) -> None: transitions to PLAYING if a media is selected; if playlist is empty, raises StateError; if at end (position >= duration), resets to 0.0 before playing.\n  - pause(self) -> None: transitions to PAUSED from PLAYING; no-op if already PAUSED or STOPPED (remains STOPPED).\n  - stop(self) -> None: transitions to STOPPED and resets position to 0.0.\n  - seek(self, seconds: float) -> float: clamps seconds to [0.0, duration_seconds()] and sets position; returns the effective position. If no media selected, returns 0.0 and leaves state STOPPED. Raises ValidationError for NaN or negative infinite values; finite negatives clamp to 0.0.\n  - set_volume(self, v: float) -> float: sets volume to clamp(v, 0.0, 1.0); returns effective volume.\n  - get_volume(self) -> float: returns current volume (0.0..1.0), independent of muted flag.\n  - mute(self) -> None: sets muted True.\n  - unmute(self) -> None: sets muted False.\n  - toggle_mute(self) -> bool: flips muted and returns new muted state.\n  - effective_volume(self) -> float: returns 0.0 if muted else get_volume().\n  - next_media(self) -> Media | None: requests playlist.next(); if a next item exists, resets position to 0.0 and sets state to STOPPED; returns the Media or None if at end.\n  - previous_media(self) -> Media | None: requests playlist.previous(); if a previous item exists, resets position to 0.0 and sets state to STOPPED; returns the Media or None if at start.\n  - select_index(self, i: int) -> Media: delegates to playlist.select(i); resets position to 0.0 and sets state to STOPPED; returns selected Media.\n  - _on_tick(self, delta: float) -> None: internal; invoked by ManualClock ticks; advances position only when state is PLAYING and a current media exists; clamps at duration and transitions to STOPPED when reaching or exceeding end, leaving position at exact duration.\n  - _reset_position(self) -> None: internal; sets position to 0.0.\n\nSemantics\n- Deterministic, headless, tick-driven: Player time advances only via ManualClock.tick calls; no wall-clock usage. End-of-media behavior: when position + delta >= duration, set position to duration and set state to STOPPED.\n- No I/O, no GUI/audio/network/filesystem side effects anywhere in core modules.\n\n__init__ exports (video_player.__init__)\n- from .errors import ValidationError, StateError, NotFoundError\n- from .media import Media\n- from .clock import ManualClock\n- from .playlist import Playlist\n- from .player import Player, PlaybackState\n\nImport constraints\n- errors is leaf; media imports errors; playlist imports media and errors; player imports errors, media, playlist, and clock; clock imports nothing from domain; __init__ re-exports only.\n\nRuntime entry (Main.py)\n- Constructs a small list of Media, a Playlist, a ManualClock, and a Player. Demonstrates play/pause/seek/next and ticks deterministically, then exits without interaction or I/O.",
    "Shared Knowledge": "The project provides a headless, deterministic video player domain. Core modules live under video_player/*.py and do not touch environment concerns. ManualClock provides a tick-driven time source; Player subscribes to it and advances only on ticks. The import graph is acyclic: errors -> media -> playlist -> player, with clock orthogonal and used only by player. The package initializer re-exports the public API. Main.py is a thin bootstrap demo. tests/test_main.py imports video_player and exercises deterministic behaviors: clock-driven progression, seek clamping, volume/mute, and playlist navigation. No GUI, audio, filesystem, or network are used.",
